{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Save Caleb the son of Jephunneh, etc.</b> A difficulty: but did not Jair the son of Manasseh enter the Land, as we expound in Sanhedrin: ״ויכו מהם אנשי העי כשלשים וששה איש״ — this is Jair the son of Manasseh, who was equivalent to the majority of the Sanhedrin; and this was after the incident of Achan. And one may answer: the Sages, of blessed memory, said that the decree of the spies was not decreed upon anyone under twenty years, and so the verse proves, as it is written: ״אם יראו האנשים העולים ממצרים מבן עשרים שנה ומעלה בלתי אם כלב בן יפונה״."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:28.373581458Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}